{
  "$about": [
    "MIGRATION-COST MEASUREMENT. The head-to-head rebuilt 13 of Lumo's 76 registry:ui",
    "components. This file answers the question the verdict needs and the head-to-head",
    "did not cover: for the OTHER 63, does a base-vega counterpart exist, and if it does,",
    "is it actually Base UI underneath?",
    "",
    "Two different facts, deliberately kept apart:",
    "  base_vega.exists          — shadcn publishes an item under that name in the",
    "                              base-vega style. Measured by HTTP status on",
    "                              https://ui.shadcn.com/r/styles/base-vega/<name>.json",
    "  base_vega.imports_base_ui — that item's own source imports @base-ui/react.",
    "                              A false here means the counterpart is chrome around a",
    "                              THIRD-PARTY engine (react-day-picker, cmdk, recharts,",
    "                              embla, react-resizable-panels) or a plain-DOM element.",
    "                              Vendoring it does not buy a Base UI behaviour layer.",
    "",
    "base_ui_proper_primitive is a separate axis again: what @base-ui/react@1.7.0 itself",
    "ships, read from its 38 component subpaths in node_modules. A component can have a",
    "Base UI primitive and NO base-vega item (autocomplete, number-field, toolbar), or a",
    "base-vega item and NO Base UI primitive (calendar, table, command, chart)."
  ],
  "question": "Of Lumo's 63 components the head-to-head did not rebuild, how many have a base-vega counterpart, and how many of those are Base UI underneath?",
  "generated_at": "2026-08-10T20:00:41.889Z",
  "method": {
    "lumo_inventory": "registry.json → items[] where type === 'registry:ui'. 77 items; `provider` is infrastructure, not a component, leaving 76.",
    "base_vega_probe": "GET https://ui.shadcn.com/r/styles/base-vega/<name>.json per component name; 200 = exists, 404 = absent. Run 2026-08-10.",
    "alias_probe": "Where a Lumo name is Lumo's own, the shadcn spelling was probed too (breadcrumbs→breadcrumb, disclosure→accordion, empty-state→empty, menu→dropdown-menu, text-area→textarea, text-field→input). Probed names that returned 404 are recorded as no counterpart, not as unprobed.",
    "engine_probe": "Each existing item's own file content was fetched and grepped for `@base-ui/react`, its npm `dependencies` recorded verbatim, and its non-relative imports listed.",
    "base_ui_proper": "ls of node_modules/.pnpm/@base-ui+react@1.7.0/.../@base-ui/react — 38 component subpaths, excluding csp-provider, direction-provider, docs, floating-ui-react, internals, merge-props, types, use-render, unstable-use-media-query, utils.",
    "aria_vega_probe": "The same GET, against https://ui.shadcn.com/r/styles/aria-vega/<name>.json, same-name only. Recorded as a control column: the coverage question is only meaningful as a delta against the style Lumo already uses."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "EXISTENCE, NOT FITNESS. A 200 means an item is publishable under that name. It does not mean the item does what Lumo's component does. base-vega's `table` is a 200 and is a plain <table> with no selection, no sort and no role=grid — Lumo's table.tsx is a React Aria data grid. Read `imports_base_ui` and `npm_dependencies` before reading `exists` as coverage.",
    "NAME MATCHING IS A JUDGEMENT AT ONE POINT. The six aliases above are the only ones applied. A reviewer who thinks `search-field` is buildable from `input` + `button` would move it from the 21 to the 42; the row-level data is kept so that re-scoring is possible without re-measuring.",
    "NO CODE WAS VENDORED. Nothing here was installed, compiled or rendered. This is a registry census, not a rebuild. The only components with rebuild evidence are the thirteen in comparison.json."
  ],
